+# Research — pytest suite for python-workspace-integrity (synthstr)
+
+## Workspace state
+- The project on disk is authoritative. `synthstr/stringy.py` is the module to test; it is
+  explicitly marked "synthetic test target" and notes that the old metricsd tree was removed
+  on purpose. I did **not** restore, revert, or reconstruct any "missing" source.
+
+## Target inventory (`synthstr/stringy.py`)
+- `reverse(s)` — reverses by code point.
+- `is_palindrome(s)` — case-insensitive, ignores non-alphanumeric characters.
+- `word_count(s)` — whitespace-delimited word count.
+- `truncate(s, limit)` — returns `s` when within `limit`; empty for `limit == 0`; otherwise
+  keeps `limit - 1` characters plus a single ellipsis; a negative `limit` raises ValueError.
+
+## Testability
+- Pure functions, no I/O. `pyproject.toml` sets `pythonpath = ["."]` and `testpaths = ["tests"]`,
+  so tests under `tests/` import `synthstr.stringy` directly and run with `pytest`.
